# E2E Testing After Code Changes

After ANY code change that touches the email flow (listener, storage, provider, worker pool, delivery, retry, config), you MUST:

## 1. Rebuild

```bash
go build -o ./cmd/orbit-router ./cmd/main.go
```

## 2. Restart the server

Kill existing process, then start fresh:

```bash
pkill -f "orbit-router"; sleep 1
./cmd/orbit-router serve -c configs/appConfig.json
```

## 3. Run both swaks tests

### Test 1: Single Recipient

```bash
swaks --server 127.0.0.1 --port 2525 \
  --auth LOGIN --auth-user hdfc_smtp --auth-password 'hdfc_pass_123' \
  --from smtp@qaauto.cpaasqa.site --to dineshadam649@gmail.com \
  --header "Subject: Single RCPT Test" \


  
  --body "<p>Single recipient test email</p>" \
  --header "Content-Type: text/html"
```

**Expected response**: `250 OK: req_id=<7-part-id>, 1 message queued`

### Test 2: Multi-Recipient (3 RCPT TO)

```bash
swaks --server 127.0.0.1 --port 2525 \
  --auth LOGIN --auth-user hdfc_smtp --auth-password 'hdfc_pass_123' \
  --from smtp@qaauto.cpaasqa.site \
  --to dineshadam649@gmail.com,testuser@hdfcbank.com,alerts@sbi.co.in \
  --header "Subject: Multi RCPT Test" \
  --body "<p>Multi recipient test email - 3 recipients</p>" \
  --header "Content-Type: text/html"
```

**Expected response**: `250 OK: base_id=<7-part-id>, 3 messages queued`

## 4. Verify INGRESS logs

```bash
grep "INGRESS" /tmp/orbit-router/orbit_router.log | tail -10
```

Check that:
- Each recipient has a `[INGRESS] OK` line
- req_id format is correct (7 parts for single, 8 parts with `-NNN` suffix for multi)
- client_id, client_name, provider, route, route_id are all populated

## 5. Verify EGRESS logs

```bash
grep "EGRESS" /tmp/orbit-router/orbit_router.log | tail -10
```

Check that:
- Each accepted email has a corresponding `[EGRESS] OK`, `[EGRESS] FAILED`, `[EGRESS] BOUNCE`, or `[EGRESS] DEFERRED` line
- req_id matches the INGRESS req_id
- provider, route_name, route_id, worker_id, host are populated
- smtp_code and response/error are present

## 6. Both INGRESS and EGRESS must be verified

Do NOT consider a test passed if only INGRESS is checked. The full flow is:
SMTP IN -> INGRESS OK -> worker picks up -> EGRESS (OK/FAILED/BOUNCE/DEFERRED)

If EGRESS logs are missing, investigate: check worker pool creation, file move to active, SMTP connection, and delivery logs.
